Flawless!

271
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:40,920
Radiant!

272
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:43,320
Premium, top-tier!

273
00:26:43,320 --> 00:26:46,320
A gorgeous, noble gem that doesn't even need polishing!

274
00:26:46,320 --> 00:26:47,920
The apex of the food chain!

275
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:50,400
A world heritage, shining bright all on his own!

276
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:53,960
The ultimate peak of the universe, bound to be somebody's greatest blessing!

277
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:57,640
Priceless, off the charts, absolute front of the line!

278
00:26:58,520 --> 00:27:01,520
Mm, miss you too.

279
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:05,320
Sure thing.

280
00:27:07,320 --> 00:27:09,680
I'll tell him.

281
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:11,880
Yeah.

282
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:14,320
No problem at all.

283
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:17,320
Okay, okay, got it.

284
00:27:33,240 --> 00:27:36,240
Thank you.

285
00:27:38,160 --> 00:27:39,080
Hello, Dad.

286
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:42,080
Oh, Gelz.

287
00:27:43,800 --> 00:27:45,360
Is Baby home?

288
00:27:45,360 --> 00:27:48,360
Baby? I saw him upstairs in his bedroom.

289
00:27:49,760 --> 00:27:52,760
Why, what's up?

290
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:06,880
Come on, I'll walk you up.

291
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:08,480
No, Dad, please!

292
00:28:08,480 --> 00:28:09,360
Let's go.

293
00:28:09,360 --> 00:28:10,520
I don't want to!

294
00:28:10,520 --> 00:28:12,440
Just go on up, go.

295
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:16,800
Dad, can you help me, please?

296
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:18,680
Go on, head upstairs.

297
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:21,680
Dad, come up with me, please! Baby is so mad at me!

298
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:24,680
Pleeeease?

299
00:28:24,680 --> 00:28:27,000
Dad...

300
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:28,440
Baby will get over it soon enough.

301
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:30,120
He won't!

302
00:28:30,120 --> 00:28:32,840
I don't even know how many times I've apologized already!

303
00:28:32,840 --> 00:28:34,440
He's being the meanest person ever.

304
00:28:34,440 --> 00:28:35,840
He's completely nuts.

305
00:28:35,840 --> 00:28:37,720
He's a rabid dog.

306
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:39,080
He's a psychopath.

307
00:28:39,080 --> 00:28:41,120
I hate him so much.

308
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:44,120
I despise him to death.

309
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:50,320
Okay, then I will go tell him for you.

310
00:28:50,320 --> 00:28:53,080
Wait, no, don't tell him.

311
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:55,640
When he's mad at me, he's terrifying.

312
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:57,600
He wants me to drop dead from heartbreak.

313
00:28:57,600 --> 00:28:59,720
He wants my whole life to be completely pitch-black.

314
00:28:59,720 --> 00:29:02,160
He wants me to never be happy again.

315
00:29:02,160 --> 00:29:04,960
So what do you want me to do?

316
00:29:04,960 --> 00:29:06,760
I don't know.

317
00:29:06,760 --> 00:29:09,760
You do know.

318
00:29:14,080 --> 00:29:17,080
I really, truly don't know.

319
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:21,560
If you really don't know, then head on home for today and try again tomorrow. Come on.

320
00:29:21,560 --> 00:29:24,720
No, no, no.

321
00:29:24,720 --> 00:29:28,040
Dad, help me, please.

322
00:29:28,040 --> 00:29:30,560
I'm begging you.

323
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:33,560
You sure you want me to step in?

324
00:29:33,720 --> 00:29:36,720
Yes, yes.

325
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:43,000
Baby.

326
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:50,560
What is it, Dad?

327
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:54,600
What are you two sulking about?

328
00:29:54,600 --> 00:29:57,600
Just tell him to go home already, Dad. I don't wanna talk to him.

329
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:02,160
Now's your chance. He's here to win you back, anyone can see he likes you.

330
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:03,760
Dad!

331
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:06,160
Stop playing hard to get and just go tell him you love him already.

332
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:08,880
Keep your voice down, Dad. He's gonna hear everything.

333
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:10,600
I am whispering, how on earth is this loud?

334
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:13,080
Just confess already so you can finally stop harboring this crush on him.

335
00:30:13,080 --> 00:30:14,520
Dad. Just leave, Dad.

336
00:30:14,520 --> 00:30:15,440
Right now I don't wanna be anything with him.

337
00:30:15,440 --> 00:30:16,080
Not even gonna let him make it up to you?

338
00:30:16,080 --> 00:30:19,080
I don't even wanna be friends! Out, out, out!

339
00:30:21,920 --> 00:30:23,400
I know it's you.

340
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:25,600
Go wherever the hell you want, bastard. I don't wanna see your face!

341
00:30:25,600 --> 00:30:28,600
Whoa, calling your dad "you bastard" now?

342
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:33,000
Sorry, Dad.

343
00:30:36,080 --> 00:30:39,080
You two sort it out yourselves. I'm gonna bounce and get my nails done.

344
00:30:39,080 --> 00:30:42,080
Dad!

345
00:31:30,560 --> 00:31:37,080
I went through my dad's stuff and found this phone for you.

346
00:32:55,120 --> 00:32:58,680
Babe.

347
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:01,680
Babe...

348
00:33:07,240 --> 00:33:10,240
There might still be info in here that you want to know.

349
00:33:11,760 --> 00:33:14,760
I really think love always stays in our phones, you know.

350
00:33:15,880 --> 00:33:19,520
But no matter what I do, it just won't charge.

351
00:33:19,520 --> 00:33:22,520
I really tried.

352
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:43,800
You know how much I care about you, right?

353
00:33:46,560 --> 00:33:49,360
Whatever you ask for, whatever you need, I do all of it for you.

354
00:33:49,360 --> 00:33:52,000
I have literally never told you no.

355
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:55,000
And look at what you did to me.

356
00:34:00,120 --> 00:34:07,280
I'm sorry! Look, I even went and tracked down this proof for you.

357
00:34:07,280 --> 00:34:13,080
Here, this phone, I went and found it for you.

358
00:34:14,880 --> 00:34:18,760
Please just unblock me.

359
00:34:18,760 --> 00:34:21,639
I'm begging you, Babe.

360
00:34:39,239 --> 00:34:44,440
Fine. You're doing my nails in return.

361
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:48,280
Fine, okay.

362
00:34:48,280 --> 00:34:51,280
It's not gonna look pretty, though.

363
00:34:51,960 --> 00:34:54,960
Toenails, then.

364
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:59,320
Come on, that's even harder. Your toenails are tiny.

365
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:04,920
Plus, I don't wanna touch your feet, that's gross.

366
00:35:16,440 --> 00:35:19,440
I have something to tell you.

367
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:24,160
Mew likes you. He told me already.

368
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:28,360
Huh?

369
00:35:28,840 --> 00:35:31,560
But I think...

370
00:35:31,560 --> 00:35:33,600
You don't need to like him back.

371
00:35:33,600 --> 00:35:36,600
He's not even all that likeable anyway.

372
00:35:38,040 --> 00:35:41,040
Oh please, look who's talking.

373
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:48,680
I just don't want you to have a boyfriend.

374
00:35:48,680 --> 00:35:53,280
Going for nails with three people is such a hassle.

375
00:36:04,120 --> 00:36:06,120
Dude, what are we gonna do?

376
00:36:06,120 --> 00:36:09,120
In Grade 7, the teacher wouldn't let us be in the same classroom anymore.

377
00:36:09,880 --> 00:36:13,120
It's because you don't study. Go rot in the bottom class.

378
00:36:13,120 --> 00:36:16,120
You studied way too hard. You should've just aimed for the middle.

379
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:19,640
Once we're in different classes, you're definitely gonna get close to someone else.

380
00:36:19,640 --> 00:36:23,360
You act like we're never gonna see each other again or something!

381
00:36:30,040 --> 00:36:32,440
Then how about we do our nails together every month?

382
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:35,440
At least we'll see each other once a month.

383
00:36:38,240 --> 00:36:39,680
This isn't asking for your opinion, by the way.

384
00:36:39,680 --> 00:36:41,080
This is an order.

385
00:36:41,080 --> 00:36:43,920
Yeah, fine.

386
00:36:43,920 --> 00:36:46,920
Okay, promise me.

387
00:36:48,360 --> 00:36:51,120
If you break the promise, I hope your nails fall off!

388
00:36:51,120 --> 00:36:54,120
Crazy, that hurts like hell!

389
00:36:54,120 --> 00:36:56,560
See? You're already planning to flake on me!

390
00:36:56,560 --> 00:36:57,480
Oh!

391
00:36:57,480 --> 00:36:58,600
See that? Look at that!

392
00:36:58,600 --> 00:37:01,000
Come here! Take this, this, and this!

393
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:03,440
Oh!

394
00:37:12,240 --> 00:37:18,000
See? Told ya. When I was about to get a boyfriend, you felt it too.

395
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:21,000
That's why I didn't want to find you one either.

396
00:37:23,840 --> 00:37:26,840
Fine, I won't have a boyfriend then.

397
00:37:27,360 --> 00:37:29,680
I'll just have you and only you.

398
00:37:29,680 --> 00:37:33,920
And you're not allowed to be closer to anyone else more than me either, deal?

399
00:37:37,120 --> 00:37:39,680
Yeah, fine. I can change seats tomorrow.

400
00:37:39,680 --> 00:37:42,080
I won't sit near him anymore.

401
00:37:42,080 --> 00:37:45,080
Mm.

402
00:38:02,080 --> 00:38:05,640
Give me your hand, I'll do your nails.

403
00:38:05,640 --> 00:38:07,360
The moment I'm not around, you don't even take care of them.

404
00:38:07,360 --> 00:38:10,360
Look, the cuticles are totally overgrown.

405
00:38:11,920 --> 00:38:15,320
Mm, but you're not allowed to request a design, okay? My way only.

406
00:38:15,320 --> 00:38:17,160
Yeah.

407
00:38:17,160 --> 00:38:20,160
Whatever you want.

408
00:38:59,680 --> 00:39:01,720
Babe, should we go grab your dad's phone?

409
00:39:01,720 --> 00:39:04,720
In case it still works. Where does he keep it?

410
00:39:18,200 --> 00:39:19,840
Go look over there, then.

411
00:39:19,840 --> 00:39:20,800
I'll check around here.

412
00:39:20,800 --> 00:39:23,800
Got it.

413
00:39:37,240 --> 00:39:39,480
Babe, is it really gonna be there?

414
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:41,440
Hell yeah, it is.

415
00:39:41,440 --> 00:39:44,440
It's definitely there, my dad saves literally everything.

416
00:39:45,560 --> 00:39:48,320
Every single scrap.

417
00:39:48,320 --> 00:39:50,400
After all this time, I bet your dad already threw it out.

418
00:39:50,400 --> 00:39:53,400
Gelz, I think I found it.

419
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:57,000
Where?

420
00:39:59,360 --> 00:40:01,160
Pretty sure it's this one.

421
00:40:01,160 --> 00:40:04,320
My dad loves keeping old stuff in here.

422
00:40:04,320 --> 00:40:07,240
Let me see.

423
00:40:08,040 --> 00:40:11,040
Holy shit, this is insanely old.

424
00:40:11,040 --> 00:40:14,040
Damn right, it has to be this ancient to actually charge it.

425
00:40:17,760 --> 00:40:22,760
Though honestly, your dad probably tossed the phone already.

426
00:40:24,280 --> 00:40:27,280
Probably just the charger cable left.

427
00:40:28,480 --> 00:40:30,880
Really?

428
00:40:43,480 --> 00:40:46,480
Huh? What is it?

429
00:41:04,280 --> 00:41:07,280
Where is it?

430
00:41:11,480 --> 00:41:14,480
Gelz.

431
00:41:36,920 --> 00:41:41,160
I think this one is my Dad's phone.

432
00:41:41,160 --> 00:41:43,560
Go try charging it.

433
00:42:03,120 --> 00:42:06,120
Shit, hey!

434
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:20,000
It just died.

435
00:42:21,360 --> 00:42:24,520
Or is it broken?

436
00:42:24,520 --> 00:42:27,360
The phone is super old, after all.

437
00:42:29,840 --> 00:42:32,000
I don't think it's broken.

438
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:34,560
Come on, the phone is ancient!

439
00:42:34,560 --> 00:42:37,040
Maybe we just wait for it to fully charge first?

440
00:42:37,040 --> 00:42:40,040
Shouldn't take too long, we can check back later.

441
00:42:42,600 --> 00:42:45,320
Yeah, we can wait a bit.

442
00:43:54,640 --> 00:44:00,960
Your face is bright red. Blushing over me?

443
00:44:02,520 --> 00:44:07,080
What? Not blushing at all.

444
00:44:21,080 --> 00:44:24,120
You sure?

445
00:44:24,120 --> 00:44:27,080
Yeah.

446
00:45:18,120 --> 00:45:21,120
I'm gonna go take a shower.

447
00:45:22,480 --> 00:45:25,480
Hey!

448
00:45:41,600 --> 00:45:43,920
Let me dry off too, will you?

449
00:45:43,920 --> 00:45:46,920
Yeah.

450
00:46:09,080 --> 00:46:12,080
Look...

451
00:46:12,080 --> 00:46:26,440
Uh...what I wanna say is...

452
00:46:27,840 --> 00:46:30,040
Is..?

453
00:46:30,040 --> 00:46:33,040
If you don't say it, I'm doing that again.

454
00:46:34,960 --> 00:46:37,960
Look, what I wanna say is...

455
00:46:43,320 --> 00:46:48,360
What I wanna say is, when are you doing what you just did again?

456
00:47:05,760 --> 00:47:08,760
Every 5%, then.

457
00:48:29,760 --> 00:48:32,760
It's at 10% now.

458
00:48:39,600 --> 00:48:42,600
Wait, you get to give multiple pecks in one turn?

459
00:49:34,280 --> 00:49:36,880
It's at 50% now.

460
00:49:36,880 --> 00:49:42,240
For the second half, can I kiss you like boyfriends? Like...

461
00:50:13,080 --> 00:50:14,880
Gelz.

462
00:50:14,880 --> 00:50:17,880
Huh?

463
00:50:26,800 --> 00:50:29,520
Look...

464
00:50:29,520 --> 00:50:35,640
I'm scared.

465
00:50:36,320 --> 00:50:40,320
Scared of what?

466
00:50:40,320 --> 00:50:51,080
I'm scared that one day we'll end up breaking up like my dads did.

467
00:50:55,640 --> 00:50:59,680
I'm scared that if we actually date...

468
00:50:59,680 --> 00:51:07,840
we'll have to break up and...fade away, like my dads had to...

469
00:51:10,920 --> 00:51:16,840
Gelz, I really do like you.

470
00:51:51,800 --> 00:51:54,800
So you're just gonna keep me on the hook?

471
00:52:08,920 --> 00:52:11,920
I'm sorry.

472
00:52:23,480 --> 00:52:27,200
You want to know about your dads that badly, right? Fine!

473
00:52:29,680 --> 00:52:32,680
Truth is, I knew everything about your dad all along.

474
00:52:32,680 --> 00:52:37,280
I was scared you'd be shocked, so I kept dodging and making excuses.

475
00:52:38,360 --> 00:52:41,360
I just didn't want you to find out, that's all.

476
00:52:45,640 --> 00:52:46,800
Hey!

477
00:52:46,800 --> 00:52:48,080
Gelz.

478
00:52:48,080 --> 00:52:51,080
Where are you going?

479
00:55:57,880 --> 00:56:00,400
I'll give you a face massage.

480
00:56:00,400 --> 00:56:03,400
Oh, Bua is already giving me a face massage.

481
00:56:05,200 --> 00:56:06,600
Baa, where are you packing up and going?

482
00:56:06,600 --> 00:56:07,560
Are you selling off all of this?

483
00:56:07,560 --> 00:56:10,560
I'm just trying to get some cash to buy a friend's concert ticket.

484
00:56:14,760 --> 00:56:17,760
I'm gonna tell everyone that you and I are dating.

485
00:56:18,520 --> 00:56:20,360
Liar, you let me sit here being all paranoid.

486
00:56:20,360 --> 00:56:23,320
Where is the trust in all this?
